cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or the measurement results, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Class Fairness in Model-Heterogeneous Federated Learning: Measurement and a Diagnostic Ladder"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Masillamni
    given-names: J Paul
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paul4805/phofl-class-fairness"
url: "https://github.com/Paul4805/phofl-class-fairness"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
abstract: >-
  A measurement study showing that client-FM hides a large class-recall spread
  in model-heterogeneous federated learning, and a diagnostic ladder showing
  that four standard interventions reduce that spread by at most 7.9% over one
  seed. The repository proposes class-FM as a reporting metric, not a training
  method.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - fairness
  - class imbalance
  - model heterogeneity
  - evaluation metrics
  - reproducibility
